From 49fd697bf24a39d31aef3d0526fffd087d8a95df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:44:34 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] A still body's feet stand on the slope under them, switched
 off until seen (patch 0078)

A body standing on a slope keeps its clips' level feet: the uphill foot sinks into the ground and
the downhill one hangs in the air. With `actionFeet` on (benilla's own, registered "0" until it has
been seen in the client) and the action layer live, each leg of a body that has stood still for
0.15 s bends so its ankle sits as far above the ground under it as the clip put it above the ground
under the body (at most 0.45 yd either way, scaled): the pelvis drops for the lower foot, and each
leg takes a two-bone turn of the thigh and the shin, its lengths kept, the knee bending the way it
bent (forward from a straight leg), the foot kept turned as the clip had it in the model frame. It
eases in and out over 0.2 s, waits out a roll, and lets go wherever the body isn't standing on the
terrain itself (a deck, a mine's floor, a building), since the heightfield is all it reads.

The legs are found once per model at bake (`PoseSource::legs`, `pelvis`): a character's knee
attachment (7 right, 8 left) rides a kneecap helper; the knee is the first bone at or above it with
a child well below it (the ankle), the hip the first bone a real link above the knee, and the pelvis
the nearest bone over both hips and SpineLow that isn't a root (the tilts own the roots). A model
without knee attachments (a boar) has none. Found on HumanMale.m2 (hips 26/25, knees 54/53, ankles
70/68, pelvis 18) and DwarfMale.m2 (31/30, 58/57, 74/72, pelvis 24); Boar.m2 none.

What it writes goes back to the animation's pose part by part, as a tilt's does. Also: the two
earlier patches' new code formatted in the workspace's 2021 style (0075's switch test, and an
upstream assertion 0076 had rewrapped).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
